text=Para o funcionamento do LTSP, é preciso alguns programas.\\%0a'''# apt-get install dhcp3-server isc-dhcp-server tftpd-hpa portmap nfs-kernel-server'''%0a%0aPra usar o ltsp-utils instalar bibliotecas do perl\\%0a'''# apt-get install libwww-perl libhtml-parser-perl libhtml-tagset-perl libhtml-tree-perl liburi-perl'''%0a%0aVamos instalar o ltsp-utils, com ele instalamos e configuramos o LTSP 4.2.\\%0ahttp://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/utils/ ou\\%0ahttps://www.idsorocaba.tk/ltsp/utils/\\%0a[@%0a# wget http://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/utils/ltsp-utils-0.25-0.tgz%0a# tar xvf ltsp-utils-0.25-0.tgz%0a# cd ltsp-utils%0a# sh install.sh %0aInstalling ltspadmin%0aInstalling ltspcfg%0aInstalling ltspinfo%0a%0aInstallation of ltsp-utils complete%0a@]%0aNo Debian Squeeze o pacote '''ltsp-utils''' não é mais oficial, por isso pegar o fonte para instalar.%0a%0a-------------%0aInstalando a partir da .ISO\\%0aObter a .iso\\%0ahttp://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/isos/\\%0aou\\%0ahttps://www.idsorocaba.tk/ltsp/isos/%0a%0aMontar .Iso do LTSP4.2\\%0a'''#mount -o loop ltsp-4.2u2-0.iso /mnt'''%0a%0a%0aAbra o '''#ltspadmin'''%0ahttps://www.idsorocaba.tk/imagens_debian_lenny/ltspadmin_conf_install.png%0aNa tela do ltspadmin vamos primeiro em '''Configure the installer options'''%0a%0aEm '''Where to retrieve packages from?''' vamos trocar e colocar:\\%0a'''[=file:///mnt/=]'''%0a%0ana opção abaixo '''In which directory would you like to place the LTSP client tree?\\%0a[/opt/ltsp]'''\\%0aIndicado manter o padrão e pra outras pode deixar em branco e dar enter.%0ahttps://www.idsorocaba.tk/imagens_debian_lenny/ltspadmin_conf_install-feito.png%0a%0a%0aPara instalar vamos em '''Install/Update LTSP Packages'''\\%0aTecle '''A''' para selecionar todos arquivos para instalação\\%0ahttps://www.idsorocaba.tk/imagens_debian_lenny/ltspadmin_conf_install-selecionar.png\\%0ae '''Q''' para começar o Download\\%0aInstalou e tecle '''Enter''' para continuar%0a%0a----%0a%0aCom LTSP já instalado, falta somente configurar...\\%0amas antes vamos editar/verificar se alguns arquivos estão como devem.%0a%0aAbra o:\\%0a'''#nano /etc/default/tftpd-hpa'''\\%0a(pode usar seu editor preferido...vi, vim, pico, emacs e etc...)%0a%0aE deixe o arquivo '''tftpd-hpa''' deste jeito...%0a[@%0a# /etc/default/tftpd-hpa%0aTFTP_USERNAME="tftp"%0aTFTP_DIRECTORY="/tftpboot"%0aTFTP_ADDRESS="0.0.0.0:69"%0aTFTP_OPTIONS="--secure -l"%0a@]%0aSalva e pronto.%0a%0aO servidor deve ter duas placas de rede, vamos usar aqui no exemplo a eth1 com ip 192.168.20.1 para o LTSP\\%0aPara isso vamos abrir o:\\%0a'''#nano /etc/network/interfaces'''\\%0aE colocar a seguinte configuração na eth1 deste jeito.%0a[@auto eth1%0aiface eth1 inet static%0a        address   192.168.20.1%0a        netmask   255.255.255.0%0a        network   192.168.20.0%0a        broadcast 192.168.20.255@]%0adepois executar...\\%0a'''#/etc/init.d/networking restart'''%0a%0a%0aPara ver como esta a configuração atual do LTSP\\%0a'''#ltspcfg'''\\%0atecle '''S''' e veja se tem tudo instalado\\%0ahttps://www.idsorocaba.tk/imagens_debian_lenny/ltspcfg_programas_instalados.png%0a%0aMaiores informações:\\%0a2.5. Exibindo a configuração atual\\%0ahttp://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/docs/ltsp-4.1-ptbr.html#AEN641%0a%0a----%0a%0aEm '''#ltspcfg''' Tecle '''C''' (configure)\\%0a2.3. Configurando os serviços necessários ao LTSP\\%0ahttp://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/docs/ltsp-4.1-ptbr.html#AEN443%0a%0a%0a'''Vamos Configurar'''\\%0ahttps://www.idsorocaba.tk/imagens_debian_lenny/ltspcfg-c.png%0a%0a'''1 - Runlevel'''\\%0ae mude o Runlevel para '''5'''%0a%0a'''2 - Interface selection'''\\%0ae escolha a interface/placa de rede que LTSP vai usar.\\%0aVamos aqui usar a '''eth1''' que antes já configuramos%0a%0a'''3 - DHCP configuration'''\\%0aaqui criei o arquivo dhcpd.conf\\%0aDo you want to build a dhcpd.conf file (y/n) ? '''Y'''%0a%0a%0aem outro Terminal/Aba faça\\%0a'''#cp /etc/dhcpd.conf /etc/dhcp/dhcpd.conf'''%0a%0a%0aE agora edite o dhcpd.conf\\%0a'''#nano /etc/dhcp/dhcpd.conf'''%0a%0a%0ae procure por:%0a[@%0aoption domain-name            "your_domain.org";   # You really should fix this%0a@]%0ae coloque o domínio da sua rede.\\%0aSugestão usar "ltsp"%0a[@%0aoption domain-name            "ltsp";   # You really should fix this%0a@]%0aprocure a linha - subnet 192.168.0.0 netmask 255.255.255.0%0a[@%0a subnet 192.168.0.0 netmask 255.255.255.0 {%0a range 192.168.0.100 192.168.0.199;%0a if substring (option vendor-class-identifier, 0, 9) = "PXEClient" {%0a filename "/lts/2.6.16.1-ltsp-1/pxelinux.0";%0a }%0a else{%0a filename "/lts/vmlinuz-2.6.16.1-ltsp-1";%0a }%0a }%0a@]%0aVerifica se esta com o ip de sua rede configurada na eth1, e confirme que linha do filename inicie com '''/lts/'''.... (se tiver /tftpboot/lts - remova o /tftpboot - pois já tem no tftp-hpa configurado.)%0a%0aEm um Terminal/Aba execute: '''ls /tftpboot/lts''' e veja o retorno.%0a[@%0a# ls /tftpboot/lts%0a 2.6.17.3-ltsp-1 vmlinuz-2.6.17.3-ltsp-1%0a@]%0aNo dhcpd.conf criado esta escrito a versão - 2.6.16.1-ltsp-1 - só que ltsp tem instalado a: 2.6.'''17.3'''-ltsp-1.\\%0aMude para '''2.6.17.3-ltsp-1'''.%0a%0aAgora faça as mudanças no '''option domain-name''', '''subnet''' e no '''filename''' -, o dhcpd.conf deve ficar assim.%0a[@%0a# dhcpd.conf%0a%0a ddns-update-style ad-hoc;%0a%0a option subnet-mask 255.255.255.0;%0a option broadcast-address 192.168.20.255;%0a option routers 192.168.20.1;%0a option domain-name-servers 192.168.20.1;%0a option domain-name "ltsp"; # You really should fix this%0a option option-128 code 128 = string;%0a option option-129 code 129 = text;%0a%0a%0a get-lease-hostnames true;%0a%0a next-server 192.168.20.1;%0a option root-path "192.168.20.1:/opt/ltsp/i386";%0a%0a subnet 192.168.20.0 netmask 255.255.255.0 {%0a range 192.168.20.100 192.168.20.110;%0a if substring (option vendor-class-identifier, 0, 9) = "PXEClient" {%0a filename "/lts/2.6.17.3-ltsp-1/pxelinux.0";%0a }%0a else{%0a filename "/lts/vmlinuz-2.6.17.3-ltsp-1";%0a }%0a }%0a#%0a# If you need to pass parameters on the kernel command line, you can%0a# do it with option-129. In order for Etherboot to look at option-129,%0a# you MUST have option-128 set to a specific value. The value is a%0a# special Etherboot signature of 'e4:45:74:68:00:00'.%0a#%0a# Add these two lines to the host entry that needs kernel parameters%0a#%0a# option option-128 e4:45:74:68:00:00; # NOT a mac address%0a# option option-129 "NIC=ne IO=0x300";%0a#%0a@]%0a%0aComplete de editar o dhcpd.conf e informe ao isc-dhcp-server em qual interface de rede vai responder/escutar os pedidos de conexão.\\%0a'''nano /etc/default/isc-dhcp-server'''%0a[@# On what interfaces should the DHCP server (dhcpd) serve DHCP requests?%0a#       Separate multiple interfaces with spaces, e.g. "eth0 eth1".%0aINTERFACES="eth1"@]%0aNo caso esta '''eth1''' pois usaremos esta interface.%0a%0aFeito tudo...execute.\\%0a'''#/etc/init.d/isc-dhcp-server restart'''%0a[@%0a# /etc/init.d/isc-dhcp-server restart%0aStopping ISC DHCP server: dhcpd failed!%0aStarting ISC DHCP server: dhcpd.%0a@]%0adhcp3 ligou corretamente.%0a%0aVoltar ao Terminal/Aba que tem o Menu de Configure%0a%0a'''4 - TFTP configuration'''\\%0acoloque **Y** (yes ) para ligar/enabled o TFTP%0a%0aEsta parte foi feito no inicio do texto...vamos continuando a instalação....%0a%0a'''5 - Portmapper configuration'''\\%0acoloque '''Y''' (yes) para ligar/enabled.%0a%0a%0a'''6 - NFS configuration'''\\%0acoloque '''Y''' (yes) para ligar/enabled.%0a%0a%0a'''7 - XDMCP configuration'''\\%0aVamos editar o /etc/gdm3/daemon.conf\\%0a'''nano /etc/gdm3/daemon.conf'''%0a[@# GDM configuration storage%0a#%0a# See /usr/share/gdm/gdm.schemas for a list of available options.%0a# Some settings can also be configured using the gdmsetup tool.%0a%0a[daemon]%0a# AutomaticLoginEnable = false%0a# AutomaticLogin =%0a%0a[security]%0aDisallowTCP=true%0a%0a[xdmcp]%0aEnable=true%0aDisplaysPerHost=2%0aHonorIndirect=false%0aMaxPending=4%0aMaxSessions=16%0aMaxWait=30%0aMaxWaitIndirect=30%0aPingIntervalSeconds=60%0aPort=177%0a%0a[greeter]%0a%0a[chooser]%0aMulticast=false%0a%0a[debug]%0aEnable=false@]%0a%0a%0a8 - Create /etc/hosts entries\\%0a9 - Create /etc/hosts.allow entries\\%0a10 - Create /etc/exports entries\\%0a11 - Create lts.conf file\\%0aNesta 4 seleções coloque '''Y (yes)''' para que o '''ltspcfg''' criar as entradas de configurações em cada arquivo e crie o arquivo '''lts.conf'''\\%0aAbaixo vamos editar algumas configurações que '''ltspcfg''' criou.%0a%0a%0a'''8 - Create /etc/hosts entries'''\\%0aSe o arquivo '''#cat /etc/hosts''' - tiver como retorno um parecido com abaixo%0a[@%0a## LTSP-begin ##%0a#%0a# The lines between 'LTSP-begin' and 'LTSP-end' were added%0a# on: Qua Abr 18 23:55:07 2007, by the ltspcfg configuration tool.%0a# For more information, visit the LTSP homepage%0a# at http://www.LTSP.org%0a#%0a%0a......%0a192.168.20.84           ws084.ltsp      ws084%0a192.168.20.85           ws085.ltsp      ws085%0a192.168.20.86           ws086.ltsp      ws086%0a192.168.20.87           ws087.ltsp      ws087%0a......%0a%0a@]%0aesta tudo ok%0a%0a%0a'''9 - Create /etc/hosts.allow entries'''\\%0aEdite o arquivo '''#nano /etc/hosts.allow'''%0a[@%0abootpd:     0.0.0.0%0ain.tftpd:   192.168.20.0%0aportmap:    192.168.20.0%0a@]%0a%0amude para ip que tu tem configurado no seu servidor. No caso aqui: '''192.168.20.1'''%0a[@%0abootpd:     0.0.0.0%0ain.tftpd:   192.168.20.1%0aportmap:    192.168.20.1%0a@]%0aSalve e pronto.%0a%0a%0a'''10 - Create /etc/exports entries'''\\%0aEdite o arquivo '''#nano /etc/exports''' - mudando para o ip do servidor. '''192.168.20.1''' Deve ficar assim:%0a[@%0a## LTSP-begin ##%0a#%0a# The lines between 'LTSP-begin' and 'LTSP-end' were added%0a# on: Qua Abr 18 23:57:57 2007, by the ltspcfg configuration tool.%0a# For more information, visit the LTSP homepage%0a# at http://www.LTSP.org%0a#%0a%0a/opt/ltsp                 192.168.20.1/255.255.255.0(ro,no_root_squash,sync,no_subtree_check)%0a#/var/opt/ltsp/swapfiles   192.168.20.1/255.255.255.0(rw,no_root_squash,async,no_subtree_check)%0a%0a## LTSP-end ##%0a@]%0aPronto....reinicie a maquina e faça os teste nos terminais.%0a%0a%0aDepois de reiniciar...vai em '''ltspcfg''' e veja o '''S''' Status (ou '''#ltspcfg -p''') e veja como esta tudo sim em: Instalado, Ligado e Rodando. '''Installed   Enabled   Running'''%0a[@# ltspcfg -p%0atput: unknown terminfo capability '-e'%0a%0altspcfg - Version 0.16%0a%0aChecking Runlevel....: 5%0aChecking Ethernet Interfaces%0aChecking Dhcpd.....%0aChecking Tftpd........%0aChecking Portmapper...%0aChecking nfs....%0aChecking xdmcp...........Found: none!%0aChecking /etc/hosts.%0aChecking /etc/hosts.allow.%0aChecking /etc/exports.%0aChecking lts.conf.%0a%0altspcfg v0.16%0a%0aInterface IP Address      Netmask         Network         Broadcast        Used %0aeth0      10.0.0.102      255.255.255.0   10.0.0.0        255.255.255.255 %0aeth1      192.168.20.1    255.255.255.0   192.168.20.0    192.168.20.255  %3c-----%0a%0aService    Installed   Enabled   Running   Notes                                %0adhcpd      Yes         no        Yes       Version isc-dhcpd-4%0atftpd      Yes         no        Yes       No '-s' flag%0aportmapper Yes         Yes       Yes       %0anfs        Yes         no        Yes       %0axdmcp      no          no        no           Using: none!%0a%0aFile                                Configured  Notes                           %0a/etc/hosts                          Yes         %0a/etc/hosts.allow                    Yes         %0a/etc/exports                        Yes         %0a/opt/ltsp/i386/etc/lts.conf         Yes         %0a%0aConfigured runlevel: 5         (value of initdefault in /etc/inittab)%0a   Current runlevel: 5         (output of the 'runlevel' command)%0a%0aInstallation dir...: /opt/ltsp%0a@]%0a%0aConfiguração baseada em outras configurações.%0a%0aAlgumas infomações sobre [[configuracao_lts_conf|configuração no lts.conf]]%0a
