diff:1297804370:1297804370:=1,366d0%0a%3c Para o funcionamento do LTSP, é preciso alguns programas.\\%0a%3c '''# apt-get install dhcp3-server isc-dhcp-server tftpd-hpa portmap nfs-kernel-server'''%0a%3c %0a%3c Pra usar o ltsp-utils instalar bibliotecas do perl\\%0a%3c '''# apt-get install libwww-perl libhtml-parser-perl libhtml-tagset-perl libhtml-tree-perl liburi-perl'''%0a%3c %0a%3c Vamos instalar o ltsp-utils, com ele instalamos e configuramos o LTSP 4.2.\\%0a%3c http://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/utils/ ou\\%0a%3c http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/ltsp/utils/\\%0a%3c [@%0a%3c # wget http://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/utils/ltsp-utils-0.25-0.tgz%0a%3c # tar xvf ltsp-utils-0.25-0.tgz%0a%3c # cd ltsp-utils%0a%3c # sh install.sh %0a%3c Installing ltspadmin%0a%3c Installing ltspcfg%0a%3c Installing ltspinfo%0a%3c %0a%3c Installation of ltsp-utils complete%0a%3c @]%0a%3c No Debian Lenny o pacote '''ltsp-utils''' não é mais oficial, por isso pegar o fonte para instalar.%0a%3c %0a%3c -------------%0a%3c Sobre Instalando a partir da .ISO\\%0a%3c http://wiki.ltsp.org/twiki/bin/view/Ltsp/LTSP-42#Installing_from_the_LTSP_4_2u2_I\\%0a%3c Obter a .iso\\%0a%3c http://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/isos/\\%0a%3c ou\\%0a%3c http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/ltsp/isos/%0a%3c %0a%3c Montar .Iso do LTSP4.2\\%0a%3c '''#mount -o loop ltsp-4.2u2-0.iso /mnt'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Abra o '''#ltspadmin'''%0a%3c http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/imagens_debian_lenny/ltspadmin_conf_install.png%0a%3c Na tela do ltspadmin vamos primeiro em '''Configure the installer options'''%0a%3c %0a%3c Em '''Where to retrieve packages from?''' vamos trocar e colocar:\\%0a%3c '''[=file:///mnt/=]'''%0a%3c %0a%3c na opção abaixo '''In which directory would you like to place the LTSP client tree?\\%0a%3c [/opt/ltsp]'''\\%0a%3c Indicado manter o padrão e pra outras pode deixar em branco e dar enter.%0a%3c http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/imagens_debian_lenny/ltspadmin_conf_install-feito.png%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Para instalar vamos em '''Install/Update LTSP Packages'''\\%0a%3c Tecle '''A''' para selecionar todos arquivos para instalação\\%0a%3c http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/imagens_debian_lenny/ltspadmin_conf_install-selecionar.png\\%0a%3c e '''Q''' para começar o Download\\%0a%3c Instalou e tecle '''Enter''' para continuar%0a%3c %0a%3c ----%0a%3c %0a%3c Com LTSP já instalado, falta somente configurar...\\%0a%3c mas antes vamos editar/verificar se alguns arquivos estão como devem.%0a%3c %0a%3c Abra o:\\%0a%3c '''#nano /etc/default/tftpd-hpa'''\\%0a%3c (pode usar seu editor preferido...vi, vim, pico, emacs e etc...)%0a%3c %0a%3c E deixe o arquivo '''tftpd-hpa''' deste jeito...%0a%3c [@%0a%3c #Defaults for tftpd-hpa%0a%3c RUN_DAEMON="yes"%0a%3c OPTIONS="-l -s /tftpboot"%0a%3c @]%0a%3c Salva e pronto.%0a%3c %0a%3c O servidor deve ter duas placas de rede, vamos usar aqui no exemplo a eth1 com ip 192.168.20.1 para o LTSP\\%0a%3c Para isso vamos abrir o:\\%0a%3c '''#nano /etc/network/interfaces'''\\%0a%3c E colocar a seguinte configuração na eth1 deste jeito.%0a%3c [@auto eth1%0a%3c iface eth1 inet static%0a%3c         address   192.168.20.1%0a%3c         netmask   255.255.255.0%0a%3c         network   192.168.20.0%0a%3c         broadcast 192.168.20.255@]%0a%3c depois executar...\\%0a%3c '''#/etc/init.d/networking restart'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Para ver como esta a configuração atual do LTSP\\%0a%3c '''#ltspcfg'''\\%0a%3c tecle '''S''' e veja se tem tudo instalado\\%0a%3c http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/imagens_debian_lenny/ltspcfg_programas_instalados.png%0a%3c %0a%3c Maiores informações:\\%0a%3c 2.5. Exibindo a configuração atual\\%0a%3c http://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/docs/ltsp-4.1-ptbr.html#AEN641%0a%3c %0a%3c ----%0a%3c %0a%3c Em '''#ltspcfg''' Tecle '''C''' (configure)\\%0a%3c 2.3. Configurando os serviços necessários ao LTSP\\%0a%3c http://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/docs/ltsp-4.1-ptbr.html#AEN443%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c '''Vamos Configurar'''\\%0a%3c http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/imagens_debian_lenny/ltspcfg-c.png%0a%3c %0a%3c '''1 - Runlevel'''\\%0a%3c e mude o Runlevel para '''5'''%0a%3c %0a%3c '''2 - Interface selection'''\\%0a%3c e escolha a interface/placa de rede que LTSP vai usar.\\%0a%3c Vamos aqui usar a '''eth1''' que antes já configuramos%0a%3c %0a%3c '''3 - DHCP configuration'''\\%0a%3c aqui criei o arquivo dhcpd.conf\\%0a%3c Do you want to build a dhcpd.conf file (y/n) ? '''Y'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c em outro Terminal/Aba faça\\%0a%3c '''#mv /etc/dhcp3/dhcpd.conf.sample /etc/dhcp3/dhcpd.conf'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c E agora edite o dhcpd.conf\\%0a%3c '''#nano /etc/dhcp3/dhcpd.conf'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c e procure por:%0a%3c [@%0a%3c option domain-name            "your_domain.org";   # You really should fix this%0a%3c @]%0a%3c e coloque o domínio da sua rede.\\%0a%3c Sugestão usar "ltsp"%0a%3c [@%0a%3c option domain-name            "ltsp";   # You really should fix this%0a%3c @]%0a%3c procure a linha - subnet 192.168.0.0 netmask 255.255.255.0%0a%3c [@%0a%3c  subnet 192.168.0.0 netmask 255.255.255.0 {%0a%3c  range 192.168.0.100 192.168.0.199;%0a%3c  if substring (option vendor-class-identifier, 0, 9) = "PXEClient" {%0a%3c  filename "/lts/2.6.16.1-ltsp-1/pxelinux.0";%0a%3c  }%0a%3c  else{%0a%3c  filename "/lts/vmlinuz-2.6.16.1-ltsp-1";%0a%3c  }%0a%3c  }%0a%3c @]%0a%3c Verifica se esta com o ip de sua rede configurada na eth1.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Em um Terminal/Aba execute: '''ls /tftpboot/lts''' e veja o retorno.%0a%3c [@%0a%3c # ls /tftpboot/lts%0a%3c  2.6.17.3-ltsp-1 vmlinuz-2.6.17.3-ltsp-1%0a%3c @]%0a%3c No dhcpd.conf criado esta escrito a versão - 2.6.16.1-ltsp-1 - só que ltsp tem instalado a: 2.6.'''17.3'''-ltsp-1.\\%0a%3c Mude para '''2.6.17.3-ltsp-1'''.%0a%3c %0a%3c Agora faça as mudanças no '''option domain-name''', '''subnet''' e no '''filename''' -, o dhcp.conf deve ficar assim.%0a%3c [@%0a%3c # dhcpd.conf%0a%3c %0a%3c  ddns-update-style ad-hoc;%0a%3c %0a%3c  option subnet-mask 255.255.255.0;%0a%3c  option broadcast-address 192.168.20.255;%0a%3c  option routers 192.168.20.1;%0a%3c  option domain-name-servers 192.168.20.1;%0a%3c  option domain-name "ltsp"; # You really should fix this%0a%3c  option option-128 code 128 = string;%0a%3c  option option-129 code 129 = text;%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c  get-lease-hostnames true;%0a%3c %0a%3c  next-server 192.168.20.1;%0a%3c  option root-path "192.168.20.1:/opt/ltsp/i386";%0a%3c %0a%3c  subnet 192.168.20.0 netmask 255.255.255.0 {%0a%3c  range 192.168.20.100 192.168.20.110;%0a%3c  if substring (option vendor-class-identifier, 0, 9) = "PXEClient" {%0a%3c  filename "/lts/2.6.17.3-ltsp-1/pxelinux.0";%0a%3c  }%0a%3c  else{%0a%3c  filename "/lts/vmlinuz-2.6.17.3-ltsp-1";%0a%3c  }%0a%3c  }%0a%3c #%0a%3c # If you need to pass parameters on the kernel command line, you can%0a%3c # do it with option-129. In order for Etherboot to look at option-129,%0a%3c # you MUST have option-128 set to a specific value. The value is a%0a%3c # special Etherboot signature of 'e4:45:74:68:00:00'.%0a%3c #%0a%3c # Add these two lines to the host entry that needs kernel parameters%0a%3c #%0a%3c # option option-128 e4:45:74:68:00:00; # NOT a mac address%0a%3c # option option-129 "NIC=ne IO=0x300";%0a%3c #%0a%3c @]%0a%3c Feito tudo...execute.\\%0a%3c '''#/etc/init.d/dhcp3-server restart'''%0a%3c [@%0a%3c # /etc/init.d/dhcp3-server restart%0a%3c Stopping DHCP server: dhcpd3 failed!%0a%3c Starting DHCP server: dhcpd3.%0a%3c @]%0a%3c dhcp3 ligou corretamente.%0a%3c %0a%3c Voltar ao Terminal/Aba que tem o Menu de Configure%0a%3c %0a%3c '''4 - TFTP configuration'''\\%0a%3c coloque **Y** (yes ) para ligar/enabled o TFTP%0a%3c %0a%3c Em outro Terminal/Aba antes edite:\\%0a%3c '''#nano /etc/inetd.conf'''\\%0a%3c e procure pela linha.%0a%3c [@%0a%3c #:BOOT: Tftp service is provided primarily for booting.  Most sites%0a%3c # run this only on machines acting as "boot servers."%0a%3c tftp           dgram   udp     wait    root  /usr/sbin/in.tftpd /usr/sbin/in.tftpd -s /tftpboot%0a%3c %0a%3c @]%0a%3c e deixe como esta acima. ...'''-s /tftpboot'''%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Bem continuando a instalação....%0a%3c %0a%3c '''5 - Portmapper configuration'''\\%0a%3c coloque '''Y''' (yes) para ligar/enabled.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c '''6 - NFS configuration'''\\%0a%3c coloque '''Y''' (yes) para ligar/enabled.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c '''7 - XDMCP configuration'''\\%0a%3c coloque '''Y''' (yes) para ligar/enabled.%0a%3c [@%0a%3c Do you want to enable gdm (y/n) ? y%0a%3c @]%0a%3c Desligar o login grafico no Servidor coloque '''N''' (no)%0a%3c [@%0a%3c Do you want to disable the graphical login on the server (y/n) [N]? n%0a%3c @]%0a%3c Veja que o padrão já não: '''[N]'''%0a%3c %0a%3c 8 - Create /etc/hosts entries\\%0a%3c 9 - Create /etc/hosts.allow entries\\%0a%3c 10 - Create /etc/exports entries\\%0a%3c 11 - Create lts.conf file\\%0a%3c Nesta 4 seleções coloque '''Y (yes)''' para que o '''ltspcfg''' criar as entradas de configurações em cada arquivo e crie o arquivo '''lts.conf'''\\%0a%3c Abaixo vamos editar algumas configurações que '''ltspcfg''' criou.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c '''8 - Create /etc/hosts entries'''\\%0a%3c Se o arquivo '''#cat /etc/hosts''' - tiver como retorno um parecido com abaixo%0a%3c [@%0a%3c ## LTSP-begin ##%0a%3c #%0a%3c # The lines between 'LTSP-begin' and 'LTSP-end' were added%0a%3c # on: Qua Abr 18 23:55:07 2007, by the ltspcfg configuration tool.%0a%3c # For more information, visit the LTSP homepage%0a%3c # at http://www.LTSP.org%0a%3c #%0a%3c %0a%3c ......%0a%3c 192.168.20.84           ws084.ltsp      ws084%0a%3c 192.168.20.85           ws085.ltsp      ws085%0a%3c 192.168.20.86           ws086.ltsp      ws086%0a%3c 192.168.20.87           ws087.ltsp      ws087%0a%3c ......%0a%3c %0a%3c @]%0a%3c esta tudo ok%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c '''9 - Create /etc/hosts.allow entries'''\\%0a%3c Edite o arquivo '''#nano /etc/hosts.allow'''%0a%3c [@%0a%3c bootpd:     0.0.0.0%0a%3c in.tftpd:   192.168.20.0%0a%3c portmap:    192.168.20.0%0a%3c @]%0a%3c %0a%3c mude para ip que tu tem configurado no seu servidor. No caso aqui: '''192.168.20.1'''%0a%3c [@%0a%3c bootpd:     0.0.0.0%0a%3c in.tftpd:   192.168.20.1%0a%3c portmap:    192.168.20.1%0a%3c @]%0a%3c Salve e pronto.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c '''10 - Create /etc/exports entries'''\\%0a%3c Edite o arquivo '''#nano /etc/exports''' - mudando para o ip do servidor. '''192.168.20.1''' Deve ficar assim:%0a%3c [@%0a%3c ## LTSP-begin ##%0a%3c #%0a%3c # The lines between 'LTSP-begin' and 'LTSP-end' were added%0a%3c # on: Qua Abr 18 23:57:57 2007, by the ltspcfg configuration tool.%0a%3c # For more information, visit the LTSP homepage%0a%3c # at http://www.LTSP.org%0a%3c #%0a%3c %0a%3c /opt/ltsp                 192.168.20.1/255.255.255.0(ro,no_root_squash,sync,no_subtree_check)%0a%3c #/var/opt/ltsp/swapfiles   192.168.20.1/255.255.255.0(rw,no_root_squash,async,no_subtree_check)%0a%3c %0a%3c ## LTSP-end ##%0a%3c @]%0a%3c Pronto....reinicie a maquina e faça os teste nos terminais.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Depois de reiniciar...vai em '''ltspcfg''' e veja o '''S''' Status (ou '''#ltspcfg -p''') e veja como esta tudo sim em: Instalado, Ligado e Rodando. '''Installed   Enabled   Running'''%0a%3c [@%0a%3c ltsp:/home/livre# ltspcfg -p%0a%3c %0a%3c ltspcfg - Version 0.16%0a%3c %0a%3c Checking Runlevel....: 5%0a%3c Checking Ethernet Interfaces%0a%3c Checking Dhcpd.....%0a%3c Checking Tftpd.......%0a%3c Checking Portmapper...%0a%3c Checking nfs....%0a%3c Checking xdmcp............Found: gdm   Using: gdm%0a%3c Checking /etc/hosts.%0a%3c Checking /etc/hosts.allow.%0a%3c Checking /etc/exports.%0a%3c Checking lts.conf.%0a%3c %0a%3c ltspcfg v0.16%0a%3c %0a%3c Interface IP Address      Netmask         Network         Broadcast        Used %0a%3c eth0      10.0.0.80       255.255.255.0   10.0.0.0        255.255.255.255 %0a%3c eth1      192.168.20.1    255.255.255.0   192.168.20.0    192.168.20.255  %3c-----%0a%3c %0a%3c Service    Installed   Enabled   Running   Notes                                %0a%3c dhcpd      Yes         Yes       Yes       Version 3%0a%3c tftpd      Yes         Yes       Yes       Has '-s' flag%0a%3c portmapper Yes         Yes       Yes       %0a%3c nfs        Yes         Yes       Yes       %0a%3c xdmcp      Yes         Yes       Yes       gdm   Using: gdm%0a%3c %0a%3c File                                Configured  Notes                           %0a%3c /etc/hosts                          Yes         %0a%3c /etc/hosts.allow                    Yes         %0a%3c /etc/exports                        Yes         %0a%3c /opt/ltsp/i386/etc/lts.conf         Yes         %0a%3c %0a%3c Configured runlevel: 5         (value of initdefault in /etc/inittab)%0a%3c    Current runlevel: 5         (output of the 'runlevel' command)%0a%3c %0a%3c Installation dir...: /opt/ltsp%0a%3c @]%0a%3c %0a%3c Configuração baseada na: [[http://idsorocaba.ourproject.org/index.php?n=Main.InstalacaoLtspDebianEtch|Instalação LTSP4.2 no Debian Etch]]\\%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Maiores Informações de Instalação no Debian e exemplos de arquivo de configuração.\\%0a%3c http://www.ltsp-br.org/wiki2/doku.php?id=debian\\%0a%3c http://oca.idbrasil.org.br/wiki2/index.php/Instala%25C3%25A7%25C3%25A3o_LTSP_4.2\\%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Algumas infomações sobre [[configuracao_lts_conf|configuração no lts.conf]]%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c Outra maneira de instalar e baixar o LTSP4.2 do mirror - http://ltsp.mirrors.tds.net/pub/ltsp/ltsp-4.2/ - com o ltsp-utils.\\%0a%3c Caso tenho boa velocidade de internet pode fazer a instalação pegando do site.\\%0a%3c '''[[debianlennyltsp42_via_rede|Instalação LTSP4.2 no Debian Lenny - Via Internet/Rede]]'''%0a\ No newline at end of file%0a
